* "German Lead 650" preamp: the six ECC83 stages of a 1990s two-channel 100 W lead amp (the ENGL E650 II; drawing "650-2", supplied by the user; the values
* marked * on the drawing are the ones given). V1A is shared; CLEAN goes through its volume P1 (R10 100k, the BRIGHT cap C4) straight to V2A, LEAD through the
* LEAD GAIN P2 (R8 100k) into V1B and on to V2A; V2A and V2B (with the Lo / Hi gain switch), the tone stack (R26 47k slope, C12 470p treble, C13 100n bass, C14 47n
* middle, R25 2.2M; the CONTOUR switch adds C9 220p), the channel relay RE4A (CLEAN: R22 220k with R28 47k, LEAD: R29 470k with the LEAD VOLUME P7), V3A, which
* is a cathode follower with the effects loop's send behind C E6 (the loop is closed: R85 10k into V3B's grid) and V3B into the MASTER (P8, behind R41 100k).
* The relays (RE1..RE5) and the BRIGHT switch are selectors here.
* Not modelled: the effects loop (send / return jacks, balance), the J175 muting transistor, MASTER B (P9, a second master pot), the clean-channel presence (R54).

* Rail: A (V1A, V1B, V2A, V2B; CE3 10u) and, behind R40 4.7k, B (V3A, V3B). Driven from the power amp at run time.
V VRAIL x 100 450
C CE3 x 0 10u
R R40 x xb 4.7k
C CB xb 0 22u

* The guitar and its pickup / cable networks, V1A.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p
R R1 in 0 1M
T V1A in p1 k1 12AX7
R R3 x p1 100k
R R2 k1 0 1k
C CE1 k1 0 22u
C C1 p1 n1 47n
R R5 n1 0 2.2M
R R7 n1 0 220k

* CLEAN: R10 100k and P1 (250k) with the BRIGHT cap C4, then R20 220k into V2A's grid (the relay's clean contact).
R R10 n1 r10b 100k
R VR1T r10b w1 1
R VR1B w1 0 1
C C4 n1 cb 220p
R SW_BRIGHT cb w1 1e12
R R20 w1 cl 220k
R SW_CLEAN cl g2a 1

* LEAD: R8 100k and the LEAD GAIN P2 (1M) into V1B, then C6 and R6 330k into V2A's grid (the lead contact).
R R8 n1 r8b 100k
R VR2T r8b w2 1
R VR2B w2 0 1
T V1B w2 p1b k1b 12AX7
R R12 x p1b 100k
R R11 k1b 0 1.5k
C CE2 k1b 0 22u
C C6 p1b n2 47n
R R14 n2 0 2.2M
R R17 n2 0 100k
R R6 n2 le 330k
R SW_LEAD le g2a 1e12

* V2A (3.3k unbypassed cathode) and V2B; the Lo / Hi gain relay: Lo adds R13 470k as a load on the coupling.
T V2A g2a p2a k2a 12AX7
R R16 x p2a 330k
R R15 k2a 0 3.3k
C C17 p2a n4 47n
R SW_LO n4 r13 1e12
R R13 r13 0 470k
R R19 n4 g2b 330k
R R21 g2b 0 1M
T V2B g2b p2b k2b 12AX7
R R24 x p2b 100k
R R23 k2b 0 1.5k
C CE5 k2b 0 22u

* Tone stack.
C C11 p2b s0 47n
R R25 s0 0 2.2M
C C12 s0 vt5 470p
C C9 s0 cc 220p
R SW_CONTOUR cc vt5 1e12
R R26 s0 sl 47k
R VR5T vt5 w5 1
R VR5B w5 b1 1
C C13 sl b1 100n
R VR3 b1 m1 500k
C C14 sl m1 47n
R VR4 m1 0 10k

* Channel relay RE4A: CLEAN through R22 220k with R28 47k; LEAD through R29 470k and the LEAD VOLUME P7 (250k).
R R22 w5 na 220k
R R28 na 0 47k
R SW_CL_V na c30 1
R R29 w5 pl 470k
R VR7T pl w7 1
R VR7B w7 0 1
R SW_LE_V w7 c30 1e12
R R30 c30 g3a 220k
R R32 g3a 0 100k

* V3A (the cathode follower: 100k plate resistor with C15 across it, 1k cathode) and the loop's coupling C E6 and R85 into V3B.
T V3A g3a p3a k3a 12AX7
R R37 xb p3a 100k
C C15 xb p3a 4.7n
R R33 k3a 0 1k
C CE6 k3a ls 1u
R R85 ls g3b 10k
R R39 g3b 0 100k
T V3B g3b p3b k3b 12AX7
R R38 xb p3b 100k
R R36 k3b 0 1.5k
C CE7 k3b 0 22u

* MASTER A: C16, R41 100k and P8 (1M); the output stays here (the power amp has C20 and the phase inverter).
C C16 p3b m0 47n
R R41 m0 m8 100k
R VR8T m8 w8 1
R VR8B w8 0 1
R R_Y w8 0 100k
